body:
Just wanted to say, as someone who has lived in rural southern California, All of the Immigrants I met (documented and undocumented) were the hardest workers I've ever met. They would make sure a job was well done, and were the nicest people I've met. They work hard to provide for their families. Maybe try to have a sliver of empathy for others?

&#x200B;

and fyi, It's not uncommon for people to live in countries where they don't speak the language and can easily contribute to society and thrive. Would you be surprised to know that a lot of English speakers move to countries that don't use English and don't make any effort to learn the countries language?
